Package: skellambrms
Title: Skellam and Discrete-Difference brms Custom Families for Count
    Differences
Version: 0.6.0
Date: 2026-08-04
Authors@R:
    person("Adam N. H.", "Smith", , "anhsmith@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0059-6206"))
Description: Provides custom brms families for a Z-valued difference between
    two paired counts, d = y1 - y2, for when only the disagreement between two
    sources is of interest or truncation via brms's resp_trunc() is required.
    Six families are supplied: the symmetric and asymmetric Skellam
    distributions (the distribution of the difference of two Poisson random
    variables), and discrete Laplace and discrete normal distributions
    discretised via CDF differencing, each with location fixed at zero or free,
    all sampled on a common SD-scale spread parameter. Stan log-CCDF functions
    are provided as stanvars so that every family normalises correctly under
    truncation. Where the pair's overall level and correlation matter as well
    as its difference, model the pair jointly instead: see the companion
    package bicountbrms.
